Owner invariants: [capture](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/capture.md), [extension apply](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/extension-apply.md), [automation apply](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/automation-apply.md), [normalization](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/normalization.md), [source policy](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/source-policy.md), [identity](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/identity.md), [desired state](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/desired-state.md), [processor](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/processor.md), [drainer](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/drainer.md), [revisions](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/revisions.md), [Booking reconciliation](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/booking-reconciliation.md), [Release reconciliation](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/release-reconciliation.md), [read projections](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/projections.md), and [observability](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/observability.md).

## Goal

Replace ad-hoc Granot webhook, extension, and HTTP apply mutations with one channel-neutral path from Granot evidence to owner-authorized Vantage facts:

webhook / extension / HTTP automation → credential-redacted **Granot Observation Receipt** → **Granot Observation** → fail-closed Registry policy + source-scoped identity → **Synchronization Decision** → later matched-Lead sync, authorized Granot Lead create, and owner **Granot Booking / Release Reconciliation** (confirm, update, or No Action).

Granot evidence never becomes an official Booking or Cancellation by itself. CRM Posting remains a separate mutation path. Approved Owner extension apply captures a `browser_extension` receipt and enters the shared processor. Approved HTTP automation apply captures a `granot_http_automation` receipt under `${run_id}:${action_id}` and enters the same claim/processor. Neither path may restore a direct Form/Call/Booked mutation bypass.

## Current service

`granotLifecycle/` is the shared runtime. The deprecated `granotWebhooks/` adapter is retired. `capture.ts` is the only webhook insert path and still does not invoke the modules below.

| Module | Role now |
| --- | --- |
| `capture.ts` | Webhook insert plus channel-neutral `captureChannelOperationReceipt` for extension/automation operation IDs. Hash/replay/409 uniqueness live here. Webhook capture still does not invoke the processor. |
| `extensionApply.ts` | Owner apply-item capture → `claimAndProcessOrPoll` → safe compatibility result. Routes stay policy-free. |
| `automationApply.ts` | Owner-approved HTTP automation action → `granot_http_automation` capture → `claimAndProcessOrPoll` → run-action receipt. |
| `normalization.ts` | Callable Observation upsert. Exact Section 10 vocabulary. No matching or effects. |
| `sourcePolicy.ts` | Fail-closed Registry read and seven-layer effect-gate snapshot. No writes. |
| `identity.ts` | Read-only Form/Call ladders, Agent assertion, Booking delegation context. No Decision or Lead writes. |
| `leadDesiredState.ts` | Pure origin-specific desired-state planner and temporal comparator. No writes. |
| `synchronizeLeadFromGranot.ts` | Canonical matched-Lead command: allowlisted desired state, Record-Link establish/attach/confirm, Lead CAS, Decision, `EntityChange`, Sheet Sync intent. |
| `createLeadFromGranot.ts` | Canonical authorized `create_if_missing` command: no caller patch; one transaction Decision + Form/Call Lead + active Record Link + Command + Changes + `form_lead.create` / `call_lead.create` outbox. |
| `processor.ts` | Channel-neutral orchestrator: identity, temporal compare, desired-state plan, gates, Decision, historical job-level Record Link. Live matched-Lead writes enter `synchronizeLeadFromGranot`. Live eligible no-match creation enters `createLeadFromGranot`. |
| `drainer.ts` | Fenced Mongo claim/lease shared by the queue consumer, five-minute cron, and Owner requeue. |
| `aggregateRevision.ts` | Compare-and-swap primitive for later consumed aggregates. |
| `bookingReconciliation.ts` / `bookingConfirmation.ts` / `bookingOwnerCommands.ts` / `referralBooking.ts` | Booking case open/refresh plus strict Owner standard confirm, explicit no-Lead Referral create, deterministic existing-Booking full update, and zero-effect No Action. Official details are one Binder plus `primary_agent_id` / optional `secondary_agent_id`; `officialBookingAllocations` derives stored allocations. |
| `releaseReconciliation.ts` / `releaseOwnerCommands.ts` | Separate Release case open/refresh plus gated Owner create-Cancellation, full Booking replacement (same official details / derived allocations), and No Action commands. |
| `trustedLeadCreateValidation.ts` | Trusted `granot_lead_created` validator (`post_to_granot=false`). Live caller is `createLeadFromGranot` only. |
| `observability.ts` / `metrics.ts` / `alerts.ts` | Section 33 catalog, closed labels, Mongo health, and seven rollout alerts. Best-effort; not business authority. |
| `creatingObservation.ts` | Owner-only Booking- and Cancellation-intake read of the selected creating Granot Observation plus credential-redacted receipt `granot_statement`. Route default is `getIntakeCreatingObservation` (Booking case first, then Release). Booking uses `selectCreatingObservationEvidence` (`preferred_booked`); Release uses `selectReleaseCreatingObservationEvidence` (`preferred_release`); both fall back to `latest_creating`. Release envelopes keep `priority_pairing: null`. Not a mutation. Routes stay policy-free. |

Admin routes activate, requeue dead letters, expose protected reads (including Owner-only candidates, creating-observation, and `GET .../receipts/live` SSE), and accept the four exact Booking plus three exact Release Owner mutations. Projections compose allowlisted DTOs; routes do not own claim, match, masking, ranking, timeline, or mutation policy.

**Contact masking follows the work, not the surface.** The Owner phones the customer on an intake, so `projections.ts` sends the whole contact there: `projectOwnerVisibleContact` for case detail, `customerLabel` for the case list and candidate rows, and the real `customer_name` on the official Booking. `maskContactLabel` survives for the discrepancy queue and outbound-SMS logging — surfaces nobody is asked to act on. `assertProjectionSafe` still bars credentials and raw transport from every DTO; it has never been a PII gate. Canonical executor / `EntityChange` live in `domainCommands/`. Live lifecycle capability includes Lead sync/create, standard/Referral Booking commands, and Release `createCancellation`, `updateBooking`, and `resolveGranotReleaseCaseNoAction`; checked-in effect flags keep them disabled.

